y":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106940#pullrequestreview-3324560103","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106940","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2025-10-10T16:13:09Z"},{"id":3338371330,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7G-4EC","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?u=e44a465cbebabb9ea2be80b59e6dc07966bef5b7&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","login":"clayjohn","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn"},"body":"To be honest, I'm a little uncomfortable with the huge amount of complexity this adds for little to no noticeable impact. I understand that this is theoretically better than the current state. But I struggle to believe that any user will actually care about the difference.\r\n\r\nThe comparison photos all look either the same, or extremely similar. And even with the ones that are different, its impossible to say which version is preferable. So I worry that this PR may just be chasing some theoretical ideal without having a strong user-focused reason to be merged. \r\n\r\nI suspect the only difference users will notice is the fact that suddenly AgX looks bad because the white point is now 1.0 instead of 16.29. ","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106940#pullrequestreview-3338371330","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106940","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-10-15T05:14:49Z"},{"id":3363022867,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7Ic6gT","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17506573?u=6e9313e254649f6dc55e92536596487ac10bf5a2&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/allenwp","id":17506573,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NTA2NTcz","login":"allenwp","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/allenwp"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106940#pullrequestreview-3363022867","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106940","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2025-10-21T22:59:44Z"},{"id":3474901784,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7PHssY","state":"APPROVED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","login":"Calinou","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou"},"body":"Tested locally, it works as expected on all renderers (including HDR 2D enabled). Code and documentation look good to me.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106940#pullrequestreview-3474901784","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106940","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-11-17T23:22:32Z"},{"id":3533566219,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7SnfEL","state":"APPROVED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?u=e44a465cbebabb9ea2be80b59e6dc07966bef5b7&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","login":"clayjohn","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn"},"body":"Seems fine to me. \n\nI agree that adding an `agx_white` property is awkward and makes the interface more bloated. But we can't really avoid it if we want to have a configurable white parameter for AgX. This sort of bloat is the reason I was against merging AgX in the first place. But now that we have AgX merged our choices are limited and we need this for proper HDR support in the future. \n\nSimilarly, exposing a new `agx_contrast` is unfortunate bloat to the interface and causes an awkward naming conflict with the existing contrast parameter. Again, there is no way around it if it really is so important to have, so the best we can do is prefix it with `agx_` to make it clear that it is a different form of contrast and hide it from users who aren't using AgX. \n\nOverall, I think this PR strikes the best balance we can achieve given that our goals ultimately require adding some amount of bloat to the interface. ","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106940#pullrequestreview-3533566219","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106940","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-12-03T07:27:29Z"}]